WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.859
Python provides multiple subprocess patterns because not every external
program has the same lifecycle.

2
00:00:05.859 --> 00:00:12.433
A simple bounded command may fit a run-style helper that starts the
program, waits for completion, and returns a result.

3
00:00:12.433 --> 00:00:16.339
A longer-lived interaction may require a lower-level process object.

4
00:00:16.339 --> 00:00:19.659
The secure choice is not about memorizing one favorite call.

5
00:00:19.659 --> 00:00:25.127
It is about matching the API to the task, output needs, timeout
requirements, and failure behavior.

6
00:00:25.127 --> 00:00:31.897
Return codes and check behavior matter because they determine how the
parent application interprets success and failure.

7
00:00:31.897 --> 00:00:41.076
A child process may finish successfully, fail with a known validation
problem, fail because a dependency is unavailable, or stop because the
application timed it out.

8
00:00:41.076 --> 00:00:50.385
The Python code should translate those outcomes into safe application
behavior instead of treating every failure as success or exposing raw
diagnostic detail to users.

9
00:00:50.385 --> 00:00:55.267
Standard input, standard output, and standard error are also part of the
security model.

10
00:00:55.267 --> 00:00:58.326
Input passed to a child process can influence behavior.

11
00:00:58.326 --> 00:01:04.380
Output may contain normal results, warnings, internal paths, sensitive
values, or unexpectedly large data.

12
00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:08.872
Error streams may include details intended for operators, not external
clients.

13
00:01:08.872 --> 00:01:17.074
Text and byte handling should be explicit enough that the application does
not accidentally corrupt data, misread output, or log sensitive content.

14
00:01:17.074 --> 00:01:20.589
Subprocess code should be simple, explicit, and easy to review.

15
00:01:20.589 --> 00:01:35.366
Reviewers should be able to identify which executable runs, which
arguments are passed, whether a shell is involved, which directory is
used, which environment variables are inherited, how long the process may
run, how output is handled, and what happens when it fails.

16
00:01:35.366 --> 00:01:41.160
If those answers are hidden in string assembly or scattered configuration,
the design is harder to trust.
